# Specify Plugin - Specify Workflow

## Overview

This plugin provides the core Specify workflow skills: initialize a project, plan a change, refine slices, build them, merge completed slices, drop discarded slices, execute the full loop, and finalize. These skills orchestrate the human-driven Specify lifecycle that the specialist plugins (Capture, Client) and target adapters (Omnia, Vectis, Contracts) build on.

**Purpose**: Drive the `plan -> execute` loop (which itself drives `refine -> build -> merge` per slice), with `drop` for cleanup and `finalize` for closing.

## Source / target adapter structure

Adapters split into two roles:

- **Source adapters** (`adapters/sources/<name>/`) supply input — `survey` (plan time) and `extract` (slice time). Examples: `intent`, `documentation`, `code-typescript`, `screenshots`.
- **Target adapters** (`adapters/targets/<name>/`) consume artifacts — `shape`, `build`, and `merge`. Examples: `omnia`, `vectis`, `contracts`.

Each directory contains `adapter.yaml` plus operation briefs under `briefs/`.

## Slice lifecycle

Slices track lifecycle in `.metadata.yaml`. The fixed loop is `refine -> build -> merge`, with `drop` as the rollback path:

```text
refining -> refined -> built -> merged
    \          \         \
     `--------> `-------> `-------> dropped
```

- **refining**: Slice directory created; `/spec:refine` extract + synthesis in flight
- **refined**: Proposal, spec, design, and tasks are validated
- **built**: All tasks done, ready to merge
- **merged**: Delta specs merged into baseline, slice archived
- **dropped**: Slice archived without merging into baseline

Per-entry `pending` / `in-progress` / `done` lives in `plan.yaml`, not `.metadata.yaml`.

## Workflow

```text
/spec:init <target>               (once per project; for a registry-only workspace, use specify init --workspace)

/spec:plan <name> source ...      (authors change.md + plan.yaml; exits at lifecycle: pending)

specify plan transition <name> approved   (Gate 1; operator-only)

/spec:execute                     (drives /spec:refine -> /spec:build -> /spec:merge per slice)

/spec:finalize <name>             (push branches, observe PRs, archive)
```

Breakouts share skill bodies with the loop and are reached when `/spec:execute` parks or the operator wants to inspect a slice by hand:

- **/spec:refine**: For one slice — extract per source, synthesize `proposal.md` / `specs/<unit>/spec.md` / `design.md` / `tasks.md`, validate, transition to `refined`.
- **/spec:build**: Validate artifacts and implement tasks for one slice.
- **/spec:merge**: Fold a slice's deltas into the baseline and archive it.
- **/spec:drop**: Abandon a slice without merging.

## Troubleshooting

### Project not initialized

- Run `/spec:init <target>` in the project root to create `.specify/` and write `project.yaml`
- Verify `.specify/project.yaml` exists

### Slice not found

- Inspect `.specify/slices/` to see active slices
- Check the slice name matches (kebab-case)

### Artifacts incomplete

- Run `specify slice validate <name>` to check artifact status
- Re-run `/spec:refine <name>` to regenerate artifacts for one slice
- Re-run `/spec:plan <name> ...` to author a fresh change

